{% set pageTitle = "FAA Pilot Logbook & 61.57 Currency Tracker — Free & Open Source | NinerLog" %}
{% set pageDescription = "Free, open-source FAA pilot logbook. Tracks 14 CFR 61.57 day and night 90-day recency, instrument currency with the IPC grace period, and the 61.56 flight review." %}
{% set pagePath = "/faa-logbook" %}
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block content %}

<!-- ============================================================
     HERO
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="relative bg-linear-to-br from-navy-900 via-navy-800 to-navy-950 py-16 lg:py-24 overflow-hidden">
  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-topo-pattern pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 text-center relative z-10">
    <div class="mb-4 reveal">
      <span class="freq-badge">
        <span class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 animate-blink"></span>
        14 CFR PART 61 &bull; FREE &amp; OPEN SOURCE
      </span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white text-balance reveal reveal-delay-1">
      FAA Pilot Logbook &amp; Currency Tracker
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-slate-300 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto reveal reveal-delay-2">
      &sect;61.57 day and night recency, instrument currency, and the grace period nobody remembers correctly &mdash; worked out from the flights you already logged.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 right-0 h-px bg-linear-to-r from-transparent via-sky-500/20 to-transparent" aria-hidden="true"></div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     THE RULES
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="bg-white dark:bg-navy-950 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4">
    <div class="text-center mb-12 lg:mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-800 dark:text-white reveal">
        The &sect;61.57 rules, tracked automatically.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto reveal reveal-delay-1">
        Every result cites the paragraph behind it. Nothing is a black box.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 lg:gap-8">
      <div class="group p-6 bg-white dark:bg-navy-800 border border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-700 rounded-xl hover:shadow-lg hover:-translate-y-1 transition-all duration-200 reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <div class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-sky-500 tracking-wider mb-2">&sect;61.57(a)</div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-2">Day passenger currency</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          3 takeoffs and landings in the preceding 90 days, in the same category and class. Counted per category and class, so being current in a single-engine land aeroplane never quietly marks you current in anything else.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="group p-6 bg-white dark:bg-navy-800 border border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-700 rounded-xl hover:shadow-lg hover:-translate-y-1 transition-all duration-200 reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <div class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-violet-500 tracking-wider mb-2">&sect;61.57(b)</div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-2">Night passenger currency</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          3 takeoffs and landings <strong>to a full stop</strong> in the preceding 90 days. Tracked separately from day currency, because the two lapse independently and usually do.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="group p-6 bg-white dark:bg-navy-800 border border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-700 rounded-xl hover:shadow-lg hover:-translate-y-1 transition-all duration-200 reveal reveal-delay-3">
        <div class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-emerald-500 tracking-wider mb-2">&sect;61.57(c)</div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-2">Instrument currency</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          6 instrument approaches plus holding procedures and course intercepting/tracking within the preceding 6 calendar months, with approaches counted as you log them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     THE GRACE PERIOD
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-navy-900 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-6 reveal">
      The instrument grace period, handled properly.
    </h2>
    <div class="prose prose-slate prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none reveal reveal-delay-1">
      <p>
        Instrument currency does not simply switch off at six months, and this is where a lot of pilots &mdash; and a lot of software &mdash; get it wrong. There are three distinct states, and NinerLog reports which one you are in:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Current.</strong> The required approaches, holding and tracking are inside the preceding 6 calendar months.</li>
        <li><strong>Lapsed, but recoverable.</strong> Past 6 months and within 12, you can regain currency by flying the required experience with a safety pilot &mdash; no instructor sign-off needed.</li>
        <li><strong>Expired.</strong> Past 12 months without the required experience, an Instrument Proficiency Check is the only way back, per &sect;61.57(d).</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Being told &ldquo;not current&rdquo; is not much use on its own. Being told <em>which of those three you are in</em> tells you whether to book an aircraft or book an examiner.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     FLIGHT REVIEW
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="bg-white dark:bg-navy-950 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-6 reveal">
      The flight review you will otherwise forget.
    </h2>
    <div class="prose prose-slate prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none reveal reveal-delay-1">
      <p>
        &sect;61.56 is the requirement that catches people out, because 24 calendar months is long enough to stop thinking about it. Mark a flight as a flight review when you log it and NinerLog tracks the expiry from there, showing you the date it runs out and emailing you before it does.
      </p>
      <p>
        The same goes for an IPC or a proficiency check &mdash; flag the flight once, and it feeds the currency picture instead of living in your memory.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     GLIDERS
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-navy-900 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-6 reveal">
      Gliders count launches.
    </h2>
    <div class="prose prose-slate prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none reveal reveal-delay-1">
      <p>
        In a glider a flight is one launch and one landing, and the launch is the number that matters. NinerLog has a dedicated glider path for &sect;61.57(a) rather than forcing sailplane flying through an aeroplane-shaped rule &mdash; a detail most logbook apps skip entirely.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you fly both sides of the Atlantic, the same flights also feed the EASA sailplane rules under FCL.140.S. One logbook, each authority evaluated on its own terms.
        <a href="/easa-logbook" class="text-sky-500 hover:text-sky-400">See the EASA side &rarr;</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     HONEST NOTE
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="bg-white dark:bg-navy-950 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
    <div class="p-6 lg:p-8 bg-amber-500/5 border border-amber-500/30 rounded-xl reveal">
      <h2 class="text-xl lg:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-4">
        An honest note about compliance.
      </h2>
      <div class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
        <p class="mb-0">
          Currency results are decision support, not authority. Regulations change and the FAA has the final word &mdash; <strong>the pilot in command remains responsible for their own currency</strong>. The engine is
          <a href="https://github.com/fjaeckel/ninerlog-api" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">open source</a>,
          so you can read exactly how each rule is applied.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     COMING FROM ANOTHER LOGBOOK
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-navy-900 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 text-center">
    <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-4 reveal">
      Already have hours somewhere else?
    </h2>
    <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 reveal reveal-delay-1">
      NinerLog reads ForeFlight logbook CSV exports and recognises the column layout on its own. Any other CSV can be mapped column by column. Currency is calculated from the imported history, so you are not starting from zero.
    </p>
    <a href="/import-export" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 border border-sky-500 text-sky-500 hover:bg-sky-500 hover:text-white rounded-full transition-all duration-200 font-semibold reveal reveal-delay-2">
      How import &amp; export works &rarr;
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     CTA
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="bg-navy-900 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 text-center">
    <h2 class="text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white mb-6 reveal">
      Know where you stand before you preflight.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-lg text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 reveal reveal-delay-1">
      Free, open source, no subscription, no credit card.
    </p>
    <a href="https://app.ninerlog.com/register"
       class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-8 py-4 bg-linear-to-r from-amber-400 to-amber-500 text-navy-900 font-semibold text-lg rounded-full shadow-lg shadow-amber-400/30 hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-amber-400/40 hover:scale-[1.02] active:scale-[0.98] transition-all duration-200 focus-visible:outline-hidden focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-amber-400 focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-navy-900 reveal reveal-delay-2">
      Start Logging &mdash; It&rsquo;s Free
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

{% endblock %}
